.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH h5i 1  "h5i 0.5.1" 
.SH NAME
h5i \- h5i unifies web development, formal verification with Lean 4, and red\-teaming around a composable Rust framework
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBh5i\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
h5i unifies web development, formal verification with Lean 4, and red\-teaming around a composable Rust framework
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
h5i\-box(1)
Disposable, confined development boxes. `h5i box` with no verb creates one from the current repository; `h5i box \-\-help` has the verb table
.TP
h5i\-ui(1)
Open the box console in a browser: one read\-only screen over the whole fleet. What each box is, what its policy actually allows, what ran inside it, and what pressed on a boundary
.TP
h5i\-browser(1)
Browser sessions: open one, drive it, close it
.TP
h5i\-plugin(1)
Install, list or remove a plugin
.TP
h5i\-project(1)
The engagement that outlives its sessions: notes, findings, evidence, checklists and reports
.TP
h5i\-app(1)
Build verified applications with h5i\-app: extract the kernel to Lean, gate the proofs, and test the spec with mutants
.TP
h5i\-skill(1)
Write or print the agent skill this binary carries
.TP
h5i\-completion(1)
Generate a shell completion script (bash, zsh, fish, ...); e.g. `h5i completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/h5i`
.TP
h5i\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.5.1
.SH "H5I BOX"
Disposable, confined development boxes. `h5i box` with no verb creates one from the current repository; `h5i box --help` has the verb table
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBbox\fR [\fB\-\-pr\fR] [\fB\-\-new\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-isolation\fR] [\fB\-\-image\fR] [\fB\-\-engine\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISOURCE\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-pr\fR \fI<NUMBER|URL>\fR
Base the box on a GitHub pull request (number, #number, or URL)
.TP
\fB\-\-new\fR
Start from an empty box instead of any source
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name for the box. Derived from the source when omitted
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Base revision, when the source is this repository. Pinned immutably.

Same conflicts as the explicit `box create` form. Without them the short form parsed `\-\-new \-\-from <rev>` and `\-\-pr N \-\-from <rev>` happily and then discarded the base: `into_command()` builds `Create` *after* clap has validated, so the explicit form\*(Aqs rules never applied. A silently unpinned base is an integrity gap in a tool whose pitch is that the base is pinned immutably.
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Remote to fetch a pull request head from
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Policy profile from .h5i/env.toml (see `h5i box create \-\-help`)
.TP
\fB\-\-isolation\fR \fI<ISOLATION>\fR
Isolation tier: auto (default) | workspace | process | supervised | container | ...
.TP
\fB\-\-image\fR \fI<IMAGE>\fR
Container base image for isolation=container
.TP
\fB\-\-engine\fR \fI<ENGINE>\fR
Browser engine for the `browser` profile: chromium | lightpanda | h5i
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the created box\*(Aqs manifest as JSON instead of the human summary
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fISOURCE\fR]
Where the code comes from: `.` for this repository (the default), or a repository URL to copy into the box. A pull request is `\-\-pr`
.SH "H5I BOX CREATE"
Create a box explicitly. `h5i box [SOURCE]` is the short form and takes the same flags; this is what it dispatches to
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBcreate\fR [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-pr\fR] [\fB\-\-clone\fR] [\fB\-\-new\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-isolation\fR] [\fB\-\-image\fR] [\fB\-\-engine\fR] [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-\-audit\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
Base revision (default: HEAD). Pinned immutably
.TP
\fB\-\-pr\fR \fI<NUMBER|URL>\fR
Base the env on a GitHub pull request (number, #number, or URL): fetches refs/pull/<n>/head from the remote, pins it as the immutable base, and points the env\*(Aqs parent branch at a local `pr/<n>` tracking branch, so propose/apply review the PR head, and apply prints the push\-back command. Needs only `git`; `gh` (optional) enriches the push\-back hint with the PR\*(Aqs head branch name
.TP
\fB\-\-clone\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Copy an external repository into the box instead of taking a worktree of this one. The box is *detached*: this repository is never touched, and `h5i box export` is the only way out
.TP
\fB\-\-new\fR
Start from an empty box (a fresh repository with one empty commit), for letting an agent build something from nothing. Also detached
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Remote to fetch the PR head from (with \-\-pr)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Policy profile from .h5i/env.toml. Built\-ins need no file: `agent` (agent\-in\-box, scoped to $H5I_AGENT\*(Aqs runtime), `agent\-claude` / `agent\-codex` (pin one runtime: only that agent\*(Aqs HOME state + API egress), `browser` (the agent profile plus headless Chrome and the agent\-browser daemon, so the agent can drive a real browser against the dev server it just started), and `default` (fail\-closed build/test confinement). Unset auto\-picks the creating runtime\*(Aqs agent profile when this host can enforce it, else `default`
.TP
\fB\-\-isolation\fR \fI<ISOLATION>\fR
Isolation: auto (default) | workspace | process | supervised | container | microvm. `auto` (or unset) picks the strongest tier the host can run; an explicit tier fails closed if the host cannot satisfy it (never silently downgrades). `microvm` boots a hardware\-isolated guest via microsandbox (`msb`) and is the only tier whose net.egress allowlist is enforced by address rather than by an HTTP proxy; it needs an image and host virtualization
.TP
\fB\-\-image\fR \fI<IMAGE>\fR
Base image for isolation=container and isolation=microvm (pre\-pulled; runs never pull). Overrides the profile\*(Aqs `container.image` and the repo\-level `[container] image` default in .h5i/env.toml. Passing it makes both image\-backed tiers candidates for the isolation auto\-pick
.TP
\fB\-\-engine\fR \fI<ENGINE>\fR
Browser engine for the `browser` profile: chromium (default), lightpanda, or h5i. Overrides the profile\*(Aqs `engine`. Pinned in the policy digest, and never falls back: a box whose engine cannot serve a page fails and names the recreate, because switching engine changes what a page is able to do
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR [default: auto]
Workspace backend (auto|worktree)
.TP
\fB\-\-audit\fR \fI<AUDIT>\fR [default: signal]
Audit capture mode for wrapped in\-env commands: signal (default) | all. `all` records every wrapped command, including small successful output
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the created box\*(Aqs manifest as JSON (the `status \-\-json` shape, plus the workspace path) instead of the human summary. Notes still go to stderr, so stdout stays parseable
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Environment name (lowercase slug, e.g. `fix\-auth`)
.SH "H5I BOX RUN"
Run one command inside a box, policy-enforced: the exit code passes through and the run is recorded as a receipt tagged with the box id and the policy digest that was actually enforced
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBrun\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a JSON envelope on stdout (receipt, exit code, timing, the recorded output) instead of streaming the raw output. Put the flag before the name: everything after `\-\-` belongs to the command. The exit code still passes through
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Environment name (slug, `agent/slug`, or full `env/agent/slug`)
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
The command to run, after `\-\-`
.SH "H5I BOX SHELL"
Open an interactive, confined session INSIDE the environment. The "agent-in-box". stdio is inherited (a real terminal), so every command the session spawns is contained by the box, not by the agent choosing to wrap each call. Defaults to a login shell when no command is given
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBshell\fR [\fB\-\-readonly\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> [\fICOMMAND\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-readonly\fR
Attach as a READ\-ONLY observer: `$WORK` is pinned read\-only, the box gets an ephemeral per\-session HOME/tmp, and no env state (status, captures, manifest) is touched. Multiple `\-\-readonly` sessions can run on one env at once (they take a shared lock); they still exclude a live read\-write session. Requires isolation=process or supervised
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Environment name (slug, `agent/slug`, or full `env/agent/slug`)
.TP
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
Command to run inside the box (after `\-\-`); default: an interactive shell
.SH "H5I BOX ALLOW"
Manage the persistent user-level egress allowlist: extra hosts merged into every container- or microvm-tier env whose profile already sets net.egress (a deny-all profile is never widened). Stored host-side under ~/.config/h5i/, outside every box-granted path; takes effect at the next `env run`/`env shell`. With no rule, lists the current entries
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBallow\fR [\fB\-\-remove\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIRULE\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\fR
Remove the rule instead of adding it
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the current allowlist as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIRULE\fR]
Host rule: exact `api.example.com`, wildcard `.example.com` / `*.example.com`, optionally with a `:port` suffix
.SH "H5I BOX PROBE"
Probe what isolation this host can actually provide (Landlock, user namespaces, seccomp) and which claims are satisfiable
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBprobe\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BOX CAPABILITIES"
Machine-readable host enforcement report: isolation tier, egress-enforced yes/no, resource-limit support, and per-claim satisfiable/runnable, so a product can adapt to the real host without scraping `env probe` text
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBcapabilities\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the structured report as JSON instead of the human view
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
Optional box name: report what THAT box actually received (its enforced policy), instead of the host\-wide capability probe
.SH "H5I BOX LIST"
List environments on this clone (the fleet view)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlist\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a machine\-readable JSON array (manifest + base drift per env)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BOX STATUS"
Show one environment's status: lifecycle, enforced policy, evidence, and base drift
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBstatus\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the raw manifest JSON instead of the human view
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX VIEW"
Watch this box's browser from the host, and take over when you want to
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBview\fR [\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-term\fR] [\fB\-\-fps\fR] [\fB\-\-assume\-graphics\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR [default: 7331]
Loopback port to bind. 0 picks a free one and prints it
.TP
\fB\-\-term\fR
Draw the page in this terminal instead of serving it to a browser
.TP
\fB\-\-fps\fR \fI<FPS>\fR [default: 10]
Frame\-rate ceiling asked of the box, for `\-\-term`
.TP
\fB\-\-assume\-graphics\fR
Skip the graphics probe and render anyway, for `\-\-term`. Frames are then sent uncompressed (about six times the bytes), because the probe is also what asks whether this terminal accepts deflated ones
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX DOCTOR"
Check one environment's enforcement readiness and structural health (can it actually enforce its isolation claim here? are its refs intact?)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBdoctor\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the structured report as JSON instead of the human view
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX SECRETS"
List the secret grants an environment's policy declares, with a dry-run resolution status (never the value: only a fingerprint when resolvable)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBsecrets\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the status as JSON instead of the human view
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX SERVICE"
Manage long-lived services declared in the env's `.h5i/env.toml` (`[service.<name>]`), confined and pid-tracked, no daemon
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBservice\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BOX SERVICE START"
Start a declared service as a confined background process
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIENV\fR> <\fISERVICE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIENV\fR>
Environment name (slug, `agent/slug`, or full `env/agent/slug`)
.TP
<\fISERVICE\fR>
Service name (a `[service.<name>]` in the env\*(Aqs `.h5i/env.toml`)
.SH "H5I BOX SERVICE STOP"
Stop a running service (and capture its log as evidence)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBstop\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIENV\fR> <\fISERVICE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIENV\fR>

.TP
<\fISERVICE\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX SERVICE STATUS"
Show every recorded service for an env and its liveness
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBstatus\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIENV\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIENV\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX SERVICE LOGS"
Tail a running service's log
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlogs\fR [\fB\-\-tail\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIENV\fR> <\fISERVICE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-tail\fR \fI<TAIL>\fR [default: 200]

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIENV\fR>

.TP
<\fISERVICE\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX PORTS"
Show the per-env dynamic port map (services with a declared port)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBports\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the port map as JSON instead of the human view
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX REBASE"
Rebase the environment onto its parent branch's current tip, re-pinning the base (use when `status` reports the parent has advanced)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBrebase\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX LOG"
Show the event log (refs/h5i/env) for one environment
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlog\fR [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 0]
Show only the newest N events (0 shows the full log)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the event records as JSON instead of the human view
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
