.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIECO\fR>
Ecosystem to refresh (cargo, npm, uv, go)
.SH "H5I BOX CACHE RM"
Remove a cache. Without --key, removes every cache for the ecosystem
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBrm\fR [\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIECO\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIECO\fR>

.SH "H5I BOX RM"
Permanently remove one or more environments from this clone: prune their worktrees, delete their code + reasoning branches, and erase their manifests. Destroys local provenance (only the `removed` event in refs/h5i/env survives). A still-live env (created/running/proposed) needs --force. Multiple names are processed in order; a failure for one env is reported but does not abort the rest
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBrm\fR [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAMES\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Remove even if the env is still live (not applied/aborted). Applies to every listed env
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAMES\fR>
One or more environment names (slug, `agent/slug`, or full `env/agent/slug`)
.SH "H5I BOX GC"
Reclaim workspaces of applied/aborted environments (worktree prune). Manifests, branches, and captures are retained
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBgc\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I UI"
Open the box console in a browser: one read-only screen over the whole fleet. What each box is, what its policy actually allows, what ran inside it, and what pressed on a boundary
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBui\fR [\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-open\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR [default: 8765]
Port to bind on 127.0.0.1. `0` asks the OS for a free one
.TP
\fB\-\-open\fR
Also hand the URL to this desktop\*(Aqs browser
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH "H5I BROWSER"
Browser sessions: open one, drive it, close it
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBbrowser\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER OPEN"
Open a URL, making a session if there is not one already
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBopen\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-new\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-loopback\fR] [\fB\-\-expires\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-dom\-instrument\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name this session, so several can run at once. A name is reusable once its session ends; the id in `\-\-json` is the durable reference
.TP
\fB\-\-new\fR
Make a new session even if one is already open, rather than navigating it
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The engagement this session belongs to. When `~/.config/h5i/projects/<name>.toml` exists it is also the scope: its grants join `\-\-allow` and its deny rules are checked before the wire
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\fR \fI<ORIGIN>\fR
Grant another origin. Repeatable. Without any, nothing remote is reachable except the URL\*(Aqs own origin
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-loopback\fR
Refuse loopback too. It is reachable by default: it is the dev server
.TP
\fB\-\-expires\-in\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
End the session automatically after this many seconds. `status` still answers afterwards, and says it expired
.TP
\fB\-\-dom\-instrument\fR
Instrument pages for prototype pollution and DOM\-XSS: inject the DOM instrument into HTML and collect what reaches a sink, for `h5i websec dom scan`
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the session record as JSON instead of a summary
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
The URL to open
.SH "H5I BROWSER PROXY"
Start a capture session: an h5i HTTP/S proxy for a Chromium to go through
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBproxy\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-loopback\fR] [\fB\-\-expires\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-dom\-instrument\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name this session
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The engagement this session belongs to. When `~/.config/h5i/projects/<name>.toml` exists it is also the scope: its grants join `\-\-allow` and its deny rules are checked before the wire
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\fR \fI<ORIGIN>\fR
Grant another origin. Repeatable. Without any, nothing remote is reachable except the URL\*(Aqs own origin
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-loopback\fR
Refuse loopback too. It is reachable by default: it is the dev server
.TP
\fB\-\-expires\-in\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
End the session automatically after this many seconds. `status` still answers afterwards, and says it expired
.TP
\fB\-\-dom\-instrument\fR
Instrument pages for prototype pollution and DOM\-XSS: inject the DOM instrument into HTML and collect what reaches a sink, for `h5i websec dom scan`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-browser\fR
Start without a browser: for a session driven only by `resend` and the plugins, or a browser you point at the proxy yourself
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the session record as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
The first target, used to seed the origin allowlist
.SH "H5I BROWSER PROXY-OPEN"
Open a URL in the Chromium a session drives. The same as `navigate`
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBproxy\-open\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The session to drive
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the result as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
The URL to open
.SH "H5I BROWSER LIST"
List the browser sessions on this machine
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlist\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Include sessions that have ended. They are kept: the record of how a session ended is the part a reviewer needs
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER STATUS"
What a session is, where it runs, and who saw its network
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBstatus\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open. A name from `\-\-session` at open time, or an opaque id. Defaults to $H5I_BROWSER_SESSION, then to the session `open` last made
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER CLOSE"
End a session: its proxy and its Chromium. Its record stays
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBclose\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-capture\-drop\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open. A name from `\-\-session` at open time, or an opaque id. Defaults to $H5I_BROWSER_SESSION, then to the session `open` last made
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
End every live session on this machine
.TP
\fB\-\-capture\-drop\fR
Delete the captured messages (bodies and credentials in full) as well. The record and the request log stay
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER RM"
Erase sessions: their records, logs and stored messages
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBrm\fR [\fB\-\-ended\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-older\-than\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAMES\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-ended\fR
Remove every session that has ended, rather than naming them
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Remove every record on this machine. A live session still needs `\-\-force`
.TP
\fB\-\-older\-than\fR \fI<DAYS>\fR
Only sessions that ended at least this long ago, in days. On its own it means `\-\-ended`, since a live session has no ending to be older than
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Say what would be removed, and remove nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Remove even a session that is still live. Its proxy is asked to stop first
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fINAMES\fR]
One or more session names or ids
.SH "H5I BROWSER GC"
Reclaim the stored messages of ended sessions, keeping their records, request logs and recon ledgers. The bulk form of `close --capture-drop`
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBgc\fR [\fB\-\-older\-than\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-older\-than\fR \fI<DAYS>\fR [default: 7]
Only sessions that ended at least this long ago, in days. `0` reclaims from every ended session
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Say what would be reclaimed, and reclaim nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER SNAPSHOT"
The page as a model should read it: the accessibility outline, with `@ref` handles the other page verbs take
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBsnapshot\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-delta\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
Only the interactive elements: what can be clicked, typed into or chosen
.TP
\fB\-\-delta\fR
Report only what changed since the last snapshot
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Go here first, then read
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER NAVIGATE"
Go to a URL in this session's Chromium
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBnavigate\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>

.SH "H5I BROWSER RELOAD"
Load the current page again
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBreload\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER SCREENSHOT"
Write a PNG of the page this session is on
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBscreenshot\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Where to write it. Defaults to a file h5i names in the session\*(Aqs own artifacts directory
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
The whole page, not only the viewport
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Go here first, then paint
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "H5I BROWSER CLICK"
Click an element: `@e3` from a snapshot, or a CSS selector
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBclick\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITARGET\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
`@e3` from a `snapshot`, or a CSS selector
.SH "H5I BROWSER TYPE"
Put text into a field, replacing what was there
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
