<\fIKEY\fR>
The key, as `Enter`, `Tab` or `Control+a`
.SH "H5I BROWSER SELECT"
Choose an option in a `<select>`, by its value
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBselect\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITARGET\fR> <\fIOPTION\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
`@e3` from a `snapshot`, or a CSS selector
.TP
<\fIOPTION\fR>
The option\*(Aqs value
.SH "H5I BROWSER SET-CHECKED"
Set a checkbox or radio to a state, rather than toggling it with a click
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
