.SH "H5I BROWSER RESEND"
Send one of this session's own requests again, with changes
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBresend\fR [\fB\-\-set\fR] [\fB\-\-set\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-unset\fR] [\fB\-\-create\fR] [\fB\-\-repeat\fR] [\fB\-\-race\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-follow\fR] [\fB\-\-reset\-budget\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-credentials\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\-headers\fR] [\fB\-\-set\-each\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\-request\fR] [\fB\-\-walk\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-session\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISEQ\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-set\fR \fI<TARGET=VALUE>\fR
Change one part of it: `query.id=456`, `header.X\-Real\-IP=127.0.0.1`, `cookie.session=forged`, `json.role=admin`, `form.user=admin`, `path=/admin`, `method=POST`, `body.raw=<bytes>`. Repeatable, in order; the value is everything after the first `=`.

A `json.` value is typed the way it reads (`json.id=99` is a number); quote it to insist on a string.
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-file\fR \fI<TARGET=PATH>\fR
Set one part of it to a file\*(Aqs bytes: `multipart.userfile=./payload.jpg`. Applied after every `\-\-set`
.TP
\fB\-\-unset\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Remove one part of it, by the same names
.TP
\fB\-\-create\fR
Add a target that is not there rather than refusing it as a typo
.TP
\fB\-\-repeat\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 1]
Send it this many times and report every sample, with a median and a median absolute deviation, for a timing test
.TP
\fB\-\-race\fR
Release the repeated sends together, for a check\-then\-act race. A burst from threads that meet at a barrier, not a single\-packet attack
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-follow\fR
Stop at the first redirect and report it, rather than following it
.TP
\fB\-\-reset\-budget\fR
Start this session\*(Aqs request allowance again before sending, for a long walk that would otherwise stop partway
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<SESSION>\fR
Send it from another session instead: the authorization test. The message comes from `\-\-session`, with its credentials dropped; the cookies, policy and receipts are the named session\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-credentials\fR
Carry the source session\*(Aqs `Cookie` and `Authorization` headers into the other session. Only meaningful with `\-\-as`
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Send this request\-target unchanged, without URL normalization
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-headers\fR
Preserve header\-name casing while retaining edits and cookies
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-each\fR \fI<TARGET=PATH>\fR
Send once per line, as `query.id=./ids.txt`, after shared edits
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\-request\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Send a complete request unchanged from this file; `\-` reads stdin.

The stored URL supplies the authority for policy checks and dialing.
.TP
\fB\-\-walk\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Walk a list of sends from this file (`\-` reads stdin): `{"steps":[{"label":"a","set":["query.user=alice"]},...]}`
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<PER_SECOND>\fR
Send at most this many requests per second
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-session\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Which session, when more than one is open
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISEQ\fR>
The sequence number to send again, as `requests` lists them
