The term, or nothing to list them all
.SH "H5I APP"
Build verified applications with h5i-app: extract the kernel to Lean, gate the proofs, and test the spec with mutants
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBapp\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH "H5I APP NEW"
Start a project: a kernel crate, a Lake project that proves it, and the h5i-app.toml that ties them together
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBnew\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-h5i\-path\fR] [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDIR\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Crate name prefix (default: the directory\*(Aqs name)
.TP
\fB\-\-h5i\-path\fR \fI<H5I_CHECKOUT>\fR
Require the h5i\-app Lean library from this local h5i checkout instead of from git
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
The h5i git revision to require the Lean library at (default: this binary\*(Aqs release tag)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIDIR\fR>
Directory to create
.SH "H5I APP EXTRACT"
Extract the kernel to Lean: Rust -> LLBC (Charon) -> Lean (Aeneas), into proofs/generated/. With `schema = true`, also write the Lean that `schema!` renders to its `lean "..."` path
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBextract\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every project under the given directories (default: the current one)
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Change nothing; fail if proofs/generated/ is not what the kernel extracts to (for CI)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Project directories or h5i\-app.toml files (default: the project the current directory is in)
.SH "H5I APP CHECK"
Build the proofs and gate them: no sorry, native_decide or axiom, and every theorem in a hand-written module uses only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBcheck\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-refetch\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every project under the given directories (default: the current one)
.TP
\fB\-\-refetch\fR
Discard the project\*(Aqs Lake packages and fetch them again, for a fetch that left them broken. Shared packages are discarded for every project that uses them
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Project directories or h5i\-app.toml files (default: the project the current directory is in)
.SH "H5I APP PROVE"
`extract`, then `check`
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBprove\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-refetch\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every project under the given directories (default: the current one)
.TP
\fB\-\-refetch\fR
Discard the project\*(Aqs Lake packages and fetch them again, for a fetch that left them broken. Shared packages are discarded for every project that uses them
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Project directories or h5i\-app.toml files (default: the project the current directory is in)
.SH "H5I APP LINT"
Check the source for what the proofs assume but cannot see: every mutating route takes an authenticated `Actor`, and no `Command` field lets the client set its own identity or privilege. Reports whether the proofs state a universal authorization theorem
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBlint\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every project under the given directories (default: the current one)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Project directories or h5i\-app.toml files (default: the project the current directory is in)
.SH "H5I APP MUTATE"
Put bugs in the kernel and make sure each one breaks a proof. A bug that survives is behaviour the spec does not pin down
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBmutate\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-baseline\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every project under the given directories (default: the current one)
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<TEXT>\fR
Only mutants whose name contains this (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\fR
Also generate mutants from the kernel\*(Aqs syntax: comparison boundaries, flipped equalities, swapped `&&`/`||`, dropped `!`, forced `if` conditions
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
With \-\-auto: at most this many generated mutants per project
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
List the mutants and exit
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<JOBS>\fR [default: 1]
Mutants to run at once. Each is a full Lean build; mind memory
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\fR
Keep each mutant\*(Aqs directory and log
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-baseline\fR
Skip building the unmodified copy first
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATHS\fR]
Project directories or h5i\-app.toml files (default: the project the current directory is in)
.SH "H5I APP DOCTOR"
Check that Charon, Aeneas and Lean are installed at the versions this h5i extracts with, and that the project pins the same ones
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS SYNOPSIS
\fBdoctor\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR]
Project directory or h5i\-app.toml (default: the one the current directory is in, if any)
